 "reason": "North Raccoon River middle reach below Sac City (HUC-10 0710000608: Sac, Calhoun, Carroll counties) plus the outlets of Camp, Lake and Purgatory creeks. This is the heavily tile-drained Des Moines Lobe headwater landscape whose drainage districts (Sac, Calhoun, Buena Vista counties) Des Moines Water Works sued in 2015 over nitrate; the North Raccoon is the high-nitrate branch of the Raccoon. It is the most upstream contiguous block of the North Raccoon that fits entirely inside one HLS tile (15TUG; the tile's north edge is ~42.44 N, just below the Buena Vista headwaters). Its 2021 CDL row-crop share (80%) is above the average of the other in-tile Raccoon HUC-12s (72%); the Hardin/Buttrick Creek block to the east is slightly more row-crop (~87%) but is further from the headwaters, so the mainstem block was preferred.",
